# SyncSpace M2 — User Awareness Bar + Cursor Overlay

## Files in this pack
- `client/src/components/UserAwarenessBar.jsx`: online members, avatar initials, names, count.
- `client/src/components/RemoteCursorOverlay.jsx`: remote cursor pointer and user name tag.
- `client/src/components/M2Awareness.css`: styles.

## 1. Copy
Copy the `components` folder into your existing project at `client/src/components/`.

## 2. Add imports to `client/src/App.jsx`
```jsx
import UserAwarenessBar from "./components/UserAwarenessBar";
import RemoteCursorOverlay from "./components/RemoteCursorOverlay";
```

## 3. Keep existing states and socket listeners
Your App already has `users` and `remoteCursors` state and listeners for `users-update`, `awareness-update`, and `awareness-remove`. Keep those; do not add duplicate listeners. The cursor data must have `id`, `name`, `x`, and `y`.

## 4. Add the awareness bar
In the main application JSX, immediately after the closing `</header>` and before `<main className="workspace">`, add:
```jsx
<UserAwarenessBar users={users} currentName={name} />
```

## 5. Overlay the cursor on the existing Stage
Find your existing `<Stage ...>...</Stage>`. Keep its existing drawing layers and handlers, but place it inside a positioned wrapper. Render `RemoteCursorOverlay` immediately after Stage, as its sibling:
```jsx
<div style={{ position: "relative", width: BOARD_WIDTH, height: BOARD_HEIGHT, margin: "0 auto" }}>
  {/* Keep your existing Stage and all its existing contents here. */}
  <Stage width={BOARD_WIDTH} height={BOARD_HEIGHT}
    onMouseDown={handlePointerDown}
    onMouseMove={handlePointerMove}
    onMouseUp={handlePointerUp}>
    {/* Do not delete your existing Layer/shapes. */}
  </Stage>
  <RemoteCursorOverlay cursors={remoteCursors}
    boardWidth={BOARD_WIDTH} boardHeight={BOARD_HEIGHT} />
</div>
```
This is a placement example, not a replacement for your Stage. Keep your actual handler names. The Stage and overlay must have the same top-left origin and coordinate system.

## 6. Test
From the project root:
```bash
git switch m2
cd client
npm run dev
```
Open two browser windows and join the same room using different names. Verify the members bar, count, cursor tags, and disconnect behavior. Check that drawing and Monaco still work.

